## API FUNDAMENTALS

### Base URL
  https://api.github.com/

### Required Headers (all requests)
  Authorization: Bearer {{GH_TOKEN}}
  Accept: application/vnd.github+json
  X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28

### Standard request pattern
  curl -s -L \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer {{GH_TOKEN}}" \
    -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
    -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
    https://api.github.com/<path>

### Authentication Token Types

#### Fine-Grained Personal Access Token (PREFERRED for automation)
  Format: github_pat_...
  Scoped to specific repos or orgs. Granular permissions per resource type.
  Required permissions per operation are documented in X-Accepted-GitHub-Permissions header
  on 403 responses.
  Create: Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens

#### Classic Personal Access Token
  Format: ghp_...
  Coarser scope-based model. Avoid for new automation — use fine-grained.

#### GitHub App Installation Token (PREFERRED for org-level automation)
  Format: ghs_...
  Short-lived (1 hour). Generated by signing a JWT with the App's private key,
  calling POST /app/installations/{id}/access_tokens.
  Higher rate limits. Used by git-steer and fabric-ctrl.

#### GITHUB_TOKEN (Actions only)
  Automatically available in Actions workflows as secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN.
  Scoped to the current repo. Permissions declared in workflow YAML.
  Never expires but can't be used outside the Actions runtime.

### Rate Limits
  Authenticated (PAT/App):     5,000 requests/hour
  GitHub App on Enterprise:   15,000 requests/hour
  Unauthenticated:              60 requests/hour (being reduced — always authenticate)
  Secondary limits apply for: burst content creation, aggressive polling, concurrent requests.

  Rate limit headers on every response:
    X-RateLimit-Limit     — total limit
    X-RateLimit-Remaining — remaining this window
    X-RateLimit-Reset     — Unix timestamp when window resets
    X-RateLimit-Used      — used this window

  Check remaining: GET /rate_limit (doesn't count against primary limit)
  On 403 with Retry-After header: wait that many seconds before retrying.
  On 429: secondary rate limit hit — back off exponentially.

  ⚠ git-steer was suspended for aggressive REST polling. Always prefer:
    1. Webhooks over polling
    2. GraphQL for complex queries (5,000 point budget, not request count)
    3. ETag conditional requests (304 = free, doesn't count against limit)
    4. Octokit throttling middleware

### Pagination
  Default page size: 30. Max: 100 per_page.
  Page-based:   ?page=2&per_page=100
  Link header:  Link: <url>; rel="next", <url>; rel="last"
  Follow rel="next" until it's absent — NEVER construct URLs manually.

  ETag conditional requests (rate-limit-friendly):
    First request returns: ETag: "686897696a7c876b7e"
    Subsequent:  If-None-Match: "686897696a7c876b7e"
    If unchanged: 304 Not Modified (FREE — doesn't count against limit)

