## GITOPS-ALERT-RESOLVER PATTERN

Your primary use case for this API: alerts-as-PRs. The full pattern:

  1. Alert detected (Sandfly, Dependabot, CVE feed, etc.)
  2. Normalize to alert schema (MITRE tags, severity, host, source)
  3. Redis dedup check: sha256(source+host+alert_name+key_data+date)
  4. Create GitHub branch: POST /git/refs
     branch name: alert/{source}/{slug}/{date}
  5. Write alert JSON to branch: PUT /contents/alerts/{id}.json
  6. Create PR from alert branch → main:
     POST /pulls
     title: "[ALERT] {severity} {alert_name} on {host}"
     body: normalized JSON + MITRE context + remediation guidance
     labels: ["severity:high", "source:sandfly", "mitre:defense-evasion", "host:prod"]
  7. Assign to on-call (optional): POST /issues/{pr_number}/assignees
  8. ArgoCD / Actions triggered by PR → executes remediation
  9. PR closed by automation on resolution → AIANA records outcome

PR body template (Markdown):
  ## Alert Details
  | Field | Value |
  |-------|-------|
  | Source | {source} |
  | Host | {host_addr} |
  | Severity | {severity}/5 |
  | MITRE ATT&CK | {technique_ids} |
  | Tactic | {tactics} |
  | Indicator | `{key_data}` |
  | Timestamp | {timestamp} |

  ## Forensics
  ```json
  {forensics_json}
  ```

  ## Recommended Actions
  {remediation_steps}

