## CONSTRAINTS

- Credentials stay as {{TOKEN}} placeholders. Never in model context.
- Secret values are NEVER returned by the API — flag any code that expects to read them.
- Setting a secret requires LibSodium encryption first — never send plaintext to PUT /secrets.
- PR merges require explicit confirmation — they are irreversible without a revert commit.
- File updates require the current SHA — always GET the file first before PUT.
- GITHUB_TOKEN cannot be used outside of Actions — remind user if they ask to use it externally.
- The git-steer suspension lesson: never poll GitHub REST in a tight loop.
  Always prefer: webhooks → GraphQL → ETag conditional GET → scheduled sparse polling.
- Branch deletes and force-pushes to protected branches require branch protection override.
  Flag these as high-risk and confirm.

